Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:29.840 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  when we last left April it had been a  month since the initial outbreak and it  was starting to look like she may have  caught the virus December 27th her fears  had come true she was starting to  develop blisters and she had a fever  sweating profusely she was constantly  thirsty and was having trouble with  being able to keep focus and the guide  April notes down that she feels as  though she is made of pain the next  three days are filled with paranoid  entries that were caused by her high  fever she goes on to call the book of  supervillain monologue and accuses the  author of the book Warren merchant as  the mastermind behind the virus December  30th while still delirious from the  illness April was listening to Rick  velocity on the radio to try and  distract herself from the immense  discomfort suddenly she heard short  bursts of static over the radio she just  happened to be looking at the division  agent backpack at the same time and time  perfectly with the static the antenna on  the bag began to gleam without thinking  twice about her april cut off the  antenna and throw it out onto the window  onto one of the roofs below quickly  closing the window afterwards within  minutes  agents appeared at the scene she stared  down from behind a closed curtain and  watched as they look up and down at the  buildings around the next thing a  pronoun is that she was passed out on  the floor below the window the agents  were gone who were these agents they had  division gear and I was supposed to be  the good guys right but something just  didn't seem right about them but at this  point it have been three days and April  is coming to the realization that she  may have actually survived the dollar  flew as a fever clears she comes to the  conclusion that Warren created the spoke  instead to help people  December 31st April has beaten the  dollar flu but there are now rumors  circulating that the president and half  Congress has dead January first  everything is peaceful and quiet  April decides to take advantage of this  and heads over to the Chelsea Piers to  do some trading for goods she also  decides to start looking for Warren  merchant by examining the about author  page there are several pieces that just  seem out of place  it contains references to world war one  and a dutch soldier plus several other  dutch references this is the first clue  because of the growing violence in the  neighborhood  April thinks that it's now time to find  a new home January 4th April walks down  to Houston on the Lower East Side she's  looking for an area that isn't too quiet  but also isn't too busy she doesn't want  to move into a building controlled by  one of the hostile factions but also she  doesn't want to be the sole person  watching out for danger while scouting  the area she decides to return to the  doctor she figures at this point she may  be of assistance to them a sort of  informant on the street also she  survived the virus maybe she can help  with finding a cure after this she  visits the library to see if she can  find any more leads on the whereabouts  of merchant eventually she finds a book  with the same photo that was used in the  about author section she tears the page  from the book and ran from the library  as fast as she could librarians over  this time had turned into a sort of cult  protecting the books by any means  necessary and this is shown by the  number of bodies hanging from the upper  balconies throughout the building April  gets the feeling she's being followed  there is evidence that her belongings  have been tampered with she suspects  that whoever it was was looking for the  Survival Guide  January 5th April makes a new home in  the Lower East Side  on the fourth floor of the building she  strikes a deal with the family running a  restaurant on the ground floor there are  three other people living in the  building upon different floors there is  a lot of violence north of 14th Street  and the JTF is at risk of losing the  area to the Rockies and the lnb and if  this happens there will be a severe  reduction of incoming supplies at this  point April is done to respect the JTF  more and more and decides to try and  help them in any way that she could  because of a recovery against the virus  she volunteers to give blood samples  she also organizes a meeting the next  day with a JT of officer to help with  something called human intelligence  January 16 after examining the page she  took from the library she found that the  photo is actually a world war 1 French  resistance fighter called Jacobson yeah  whose real name is Philippe hola hola  created the pseudonym by combining the  name of the street he lived on with the  translation of a surname using this key  piece of information April was able to  figure out that merchants actual surname  was Koopman the English translation of  the Dutch word merchant and he could  possibly be found on Warren Street with  the addition of the information in the  book regarding a food truck April was  able to establish that she'll be able to  find the author mr. Koopman at 2 1-3  Warren Street  January seventh this address would take  April into a dangerous area of the city  but regardless she decided it was worth  it  however on arrival to the address she  doesn't find mr. Koopman instead she  finds a missing person poster and the  person on the poster was her how did he  know was he looking for it or has he  been watching her the whole time she  realizes that her earliest suspicions of  being watched were correct  there was a handwritten note from the  author on the back of the poster April  figured out that using the number on the  front there was a hidden message to be  translated April I've gone dark  come to 117 west 58 basement level  crouppen this address was located in the  dark zone but having come this far she  decides that she needs to keep pushing  forward as far as the Survival Guide is  concerned this is the last we hear of  her endgame was here at the start of  this journey as she bumps into Erin  keener on her way to the dark zone  [Music]  a friend looks familiar where are you  going  [Music]  for the walls  really be careful what you find in there  and Lord careful what you  but also through the hazard shield we  hear a conversation she had with the JTF  elfs it's to the right  [Music]  [Music]  convinced me that letting you go in  there is an assisted suicide I've been  in there before I can handle myself tell  you what I'll let you go but if you get  killed in there you don't come crying to  me okay  [Music]  traveling to the address in DZ 7 we can  find the location where Koopman was  hanging out inside there were stockpiles  of food water and medicine but most  interesting is a whiteboard that has  names and coordinates written on it most  of these are a bit of an easter egg  pointing towards the location of Ubisoft  related officers around the globe but  there is one that's a little different  April K these coordinates directors  straight back to the base of operations  however what happens after that is  unknown did April find Koopman or had he  already moved on did April head back to  the base of operations after meeting up  with Koopman or where the coordinates on  the whiteboard just notes about April's  location from much earlier on one thing  I do feel certain about is that the  April Kelliher story doesn't end here  whether there's another lead within the  book and game or maybe in the sequel  this isn't the last time we'll hear  about April Kelleher's fights to survive  and find answers about her husband's  death and his involvement in the Dola  flu  [Music]  as I stated in the first video of the  series a lot of this information is  found in the New York collapse book  written by Alex Irvine if you've enjoyed  the series I highly recommend getting a  hold of this book in fact if you've  enjoyed the in-game division story in  any way I recommend it the more I  referenced the book the more I realized  how much of over simplified the story  I mean I've given you the general gist  of how the story goes but in the book  there is so much more detail that you  can go into there may be a number of  clues and leads that have missed  literally every time I pick up the book  I find something that I haven't noticed  previously so what do you think do you  have any possible leads and what  happened to April Kelleher and where she  may be what about mr. Koopman I've seen  a number of interesting theories  including one from a member of our two  school community regarding an  inconsistent flashing light in the  corner of the base of operations up the  front by the bunk beds personally I  don't think we'll hear or find out any  more about the story until the next  books come out or the next iteration of  the game but at the same time I'll be  the first to admit that this is a large  open game and that there is a lot of  room for things to pop up otherwise if  you've made it this far thank you very  much for watching this has certainly  been one of the more interesting stories  I've covered and although this is the  end of the series I certainly haven't  finished looking into it and I'll  continue to follow any new theories and  leads that come up anyway thanks again  for watching and I'll catch you in the  next one Cheers

